arg "The AGENTS.md of your working folder:\n\nRun make test before you finish.\n\nYou work through AgentBus, in session s1. A turn is one message to you, your reply and your changes.\nYour folder is usually your session's own copy of the person's folder. Your edits stay in the copy. They reach the person's folder only when a turn is applied.\nUse the agentbus MCP tools to ask other saved agents (any vendor) for work (ask_agent) or to have one review a turn (review_turn). AgentBus agents are saved setups across vendors, not your harness's own agents or subagents.\nTo read turns and their diffs, search this session, or stop a turn, use agentbus-api (GET /api/v0/turns, GET /api/v0/turns/T/diff, POST /api/v0/turns/T/stop). A short guide to every route is at agentbus-api GET /docs/llms.txt.\nThe person applies your changes to their folder; you cannot.\nWork you ask for comes back to you as a later turn: do not wait for it.\n\nAnother agent asked for this work, from session s0, turn t_0 (also in AGENTBUS_ASKED_BY_SESSION and AGENTBUS_ASKED_BY_TURN, and in your own turn's origin in agentbus-api GET \"/api/v0/turns\"). Your folder may not hold its changes. To read what that turn changed, with each file's diff, run:\nagentbus-api GET \"/api/v0/turns/t_0/changes?session=s0\"\nIts changes are empty while that turn still runs; read it again once its state is no longer running. That session's earlier turns: agentbus-api GET \"/api/v0/turns?session=s0\""
arg "--allowedTools"
arg "Edit(/<folder>/**),Bash,mcp__agentbus"
arg "--mcp-config"
arg "{\"mcpServers\":{\"agentbus\":{\"headers\":{\"Authorization\":\"Bearer ${AGENTBUS_TOKEN}\"},\"type\":\"http\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/v0/mcp\"}}}"
arg "--no-chrome"
arg "--disallowedTools"
arg "Edit(/<data>/permissions.toml),Edit(/<data>/instructions.md),Edit(/<data>/agents.json),Task,Agent,Workflow,ListAgents,SendMessage"
arg "--"
arg "one"
env "AGENTBUS_ASKED_BY_SESSION=s0"
env "AGENTBUS_ASKED_BY_TURN=t_0"
env "AGENTBUS_LAUNCH_DIR=<launch>"
env "AGENTBUS_TOKEN=<token>
env "AGENTBUS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787"
env "HOME=<home>"
env "PATH=<data>/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
env "PWD=<folder>"
cwd <folder>
turn.started agent="claude" continuity="" replay_from="" model="" context=""
context.added agents_md=71 instructions=844 asked_by=520 mcp_instructions=327
run.ended resume_id="sid-0"
